        "## Task 2 — Box plot: listing activity by borough\n",
        "\n",
        "**What to build:** A **horizontal box plot** comparing listing activity (reviews per month) across London boroughs — reviews per month is a proxy for how frequently a listing is booked.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Requirements:**\n",
        "- Horizontal orientation (borough names are long)\n",
        "- Sorted by median reviews per month (most active at top)\n",
        "- Highlight the **two most active** boroughs in a different colour\n",
        "- Outliers shown as individual points\n",
        "- Insight title naming the two busiest boroughs\n",
        "\n",
        "> 💡 Some listings have zero reviews — these are new or inactive listings. Filter them out with before plotting"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "MctH3bOzec-r"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Task 2\n",
        "# Borough column name differs between Airbnb exports — pick whichever exists\n",
        "borough_col = next(c for c in ['neighbourhood', 'neighbourhood_cleansed', 'borough'] if c in df.columns)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Remove new/inactive listings (zero or missing reviews)\n",
        "act = df[df['reviews_per_month'] > 0].copy()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Order boroughs by median activity\n",
        "order = act.groupby(borough_col)['reviews_per_month'].median().sort_values(ascending=False)\n",
        "top2 = order.index[:2].tolist()\n",
        "\n",
        "# Colour = highlight (top 2 vs the rest)\n",
        "act['group'] = np.where(act[borough_col].isin(top2), 'Two most active', 'Other boroughs')\n",
        "\n",
        "fig2 = px.box(\n",
        "    act, x='reviews_per_month', y=borough_col, color='group',\n",
        "    orientation='h', points='outliers',\n",
        "    # px puts the first category at the top for horizontal charts → most active first\n",
        "    category_orders={borough_col: order.index.tolist(),\n",
        "                     'group': ['Two most active', 'Other boroughs']},\n",
        "    color_discrete_map={'Two most active': '#d62728', 'Other boroughs': '#b0b0b0'},\n",
        "    labels={'reviews_per_month': 'Reviews per month (booking-activity proxy)', borough_col: ''},\n",
        "    title=(f\"{top2[0]} and {top2[1]} are London's busiest boroughs — \"\n",
        "           f\"median {order.iloc[0]:.2f} and {order.iloc[1]:.2f} reviews/month\")\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# London-wide median reference line\n",
        "overall_med = act['reviews_per_month'].median()\n",
        "fig2.add_vline(x=overall_med, line_dash='dash', line_color='black',\n",
        "               annotation_text=f\"London median: {overall_med:.2f}\",\n",
        "               annotation_position='top right')\n",
        "\n",
        "fig2.add_annotation(xref='paper', yref='paper', x=1, y=-0.06, showarrow=False,\n",
        "                    xanchor='right', font=dict(size=11, color='grey'),\n",
        "                    text=f\"Listings with zero reviews excluded (n = {len(act):,} active listings)\")\n",
        "\n",
        "fig2.update_layout(boxmode='overlay',      # stop the two colour groups being offset\n",
        "                   height=max(500, 28 * order.size),\n",
        "                   legend_title='', template='simple_white')\n",
        "fig2.show()\n"
      ],
